{
  "_comment": [
    "Controlled tag vocabulary for the cookbook. Tags are a digital-edition",
    "navigation aid (the print build strips them), so the goal is discovery:",
    "every canonical tag should plausibly appear on more than one recipe.",
    "",
    "Before this file existed there were 1432 distinct tags, 75% of them used",
    "exactly once, and per-recipe counts ranged from 6 to 106. That is the",
    "signature of per-recipe generation with no shared vocabulary.",
    "",
    "RULES",
    "1. Only tags in 'facets' may appear on a recipe.",
    "2. 'aliases' maps a retired spelling or synonym onto its canonical tag.",
    "3. 'drop' removes tags that carry no navigational value, including any that",
    "   duplicate a header field (Effort, Maturity, Oversight).",
    "4. Anything not in facets or aliases is dropped.",
    "5. There is NO per-recipe cap. An earlier revision capped at 16 and discarded",
    "   370 valid canonical tags from the 31 most complex recipes, including",
    "   high-value navigation tags like hipaa, phi-handling, audit-trail and",
    "   healthlake. Tags cost nothing in print (they are stripped) and more",
    "   canonical tags mean better discovery, so density is a presentation concern",
    "   for CSS, not a reason to delete data."
  ],
